      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). At that level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nSome possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg** doses at some other frequency.\n\nCan you tell me the dose and frequency you want? If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, let me know and add a clinical justification. I'd suggest confirming it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
